{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Extend the existing Spring XD code base (admin server, container, module model, Kafka message bus/binder) rather than building a new runtime; development targets the JDK level already supported by that code base.",
    "For U2, implement starting-offset control via a deployment-time property on the Kafka source (e.g., kafka.startingOffset=earliest|latest|<explicit offset>) that is applied only at stream deployment.",
    "For U2, persist consumer progress using Kafka's committed offset storage (consumer group offsets) so offsets survive module crashes; modules resume from the last committed offset after a crash or restart.",
    "For U2, resolve the open TBD as follows: undeploying and redeploying without an explicit starting offset resumes from the last committed offset, while redeploying with an explicit starting offset resets and re-reads from that offset.",
    "For U3 and U4, use static partition assignment (KafkaConsumer.assign with explicit TopicPartitions computed from module instanceIndex/instanceCount and stream partitioning properties) instead of group-based subscription, so no consumer-group rebalancing occurs on deploy, crash, or redeploy.",
    "For U4, extend the Kafka message bus binder to compute a deterministic node-to-partition mapping at deployment time from the stream's partition count and the number of provisioned container nodes, and to bind producers/consumers to fixed partitions.",
    "For U6, build the reactor-stream processor module on Project Reactor's stream API, implementing time windows via windowing operations and evaluating min/avg-style aggregations through configurable SpEL expressions on extracted fields.",
    "For U7, implement microbatching as a configurable buffering stage in the source module/message bus path that accumulates messages and emits a batch when batchInterval elapses, preserving message ordering within a partition.",
    "For U5, treat Spark integration as a research spike: produce a proof of concept and a written design recommendation only; no production Spark module is included in this increment.",
    "For U8, automate Rackspace provisioning (Kafka cluster, ZooKeeper, XD cluster nodes) with repeatable scripts and use standard Kafka performance tools plus XD stream scenarios for benchmarking.",
    "Use embedded Kafka/ZooKeeper-based integration tests in the build for offset and partitioning behavior, plus multi-container integration tests for pre-allocation and crash/redeploy scenarios."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "An existing Spring XD code base with a working Kafka message bus, module registry, build system, and CI is available as the starting point; no greenfield infrastructure or framework setup is required.",
    "One developer (the estimator) performs all work, including design, coding, testing, documentation, and infrastructure tasks; all figures are effort in work-hours, not elapsed calendar time.",
    "A work-hour is one hour of focused work by a single developer; estimates exclude organizational overhead such as meetings unrelated to the increment, vacations, and wait time for external approvals.",
    "Kafka and ZooKeeper clusters are available for development and testing (embedded instances for automated tests; a multi-node cluster for performance work via U8).",
    "The U2 TBD question is resolved by the documented design decision: without an explicit starting offset, redeployed streams resume from the last committed offset.",
    "U5 scope is limited to investigation, a proof of concept, and a design recommendation; full production Spark support is a future increment and is not estimated here.",
    "U6 scope covers the reactor-stream processor module with time-window operations (e.g., min, avg via expressions); the 'integration with Spark streaming and reactor' example is covered only by the U5 proof of concept.",
    "U1 documentation is delivered as wiki pages covering the new Kafka source options, partition pre-allocation, microbatching, the reactor-stream module, and the performance infrastructure.",
    "Estimates include unit tests, integration tests, code review rework, and defect fixing within each activity; they exclude production deployment and ongoing operations.",
    "No changes to the public XD DSL grammar are required beyond adding module/deployment properties; existing stream definitions continue to work unchanged."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment requirements analysis and architecture design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze user stories U1-U8 against the existing Spring XD code base, define the overall design for offset management, static partition allocation, microbatching, and the reactor-stream module, and produce design notes that guide implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Design Kafka starting offset management (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Design the deployment-time starting offset property, offset reset semantics, and crash-recovery behavior using committed offsets, including the undeploy/redeploy resolution of the open TBD.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement starting offset control in Kafka source (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the starting offset configuration on the Kafka source module so that the offset is applied when a stream is deployed, including explicit offset, earliest, and latest options.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement offset progress persistence and crash recovery (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement offset commit/tracking logic so that consumed progress survives module crashes for a running stream and is correctly reset when a stream is redeployed with a specific starting offset.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Offset control tests (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests and embedded-Kafka integration tests covering initial deployment offsets, crash recovery, redeploy without offset (resume), and redeploy with explicit offset (replay).",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Design static partition pre-allocation for Kafka sources (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Design how XD pre-allocates topic partitions among Kafka source module instances at deployment time using instance count/index properties and static assignment instead of consumer-group rebalancing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement source partition pre-allocation (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Implement deterministic partition assignment for Kafka source module instances at deploy time, including validation of partition counts versus instance counts and disabling group rebalancing for these consumers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 56
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Source partitioning tests (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Write tests for multi-instance source deployments verifying correct partition allocation, no rebalancing on instance changes, and error handling for invalid configurations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Design message bus partition pre-allocation (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Design the deterministic node-to-partition mapping for the Kafka message bus so producer and consumer bindings are fixed at deployment time and unaffected by container crashes or redeployments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Implement message bus partition pre-allocation (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement static partition allocation in the Kafka message bus binder, including fixed partition routing for producers and static consumer assignment computed from deployment properties and provisioned nodes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 72
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Message bus partitioning tests (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests covering pre-allocated bindings across multiple containers, container crash and restart without rebalancing, and stream redeployment scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Spark research and proof of concept (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Investigate Spark and Spark Streaming integration options for XD, build a proof of concept demonstrating processing of XD-ingested data with Spark, and evaluate feasibility, performance characteristics, and operational complexity.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "POC evaluation report and design recommendation (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Document POC findings, compare candidate designs, and produce a written recommendation for the appropriate Spark design and implementation approach for XD.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Design reactor-stream processor module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Design the reactor-stream processor module contract, including timeWindow configuration, field extraction from payloads, expression-based aggregations (min, avg), and output format.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Implement reactor-stream time-window processor (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the processor module using the Reactor stream API with time-window operations and configurable SpEL-based aggregations, and register it as an XD processor module usable in stream definitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "Reactor-stream module tests and samples (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for windowing and aggregation behavior and create working sample streams (e.g., http | reactor-stream --timeWindow=10s --field=payload.sensorData --expressions=min,avg).",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Design microbatching approach (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Design the batchInterval-based microbatching mechanism, including buffering semantics, batch emission triggers, ordering guarantees, and configuration surface for source modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Implement batchInterval microbatching (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement configurable microbatching in the ingestion path so that streams such as 'http --batchInterval=10 | log' buffer messages and emit them as batches at the configured interval.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Microbatching tests and throughput validation (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Write tests for batching correctness (intervals, boundaries, ordering) and validate throughput improvements against non-batched ingestion.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Provision Rackspace performance environment (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Create automation scripts to provision and configure the Rackspace test environment, including Kafka/ZooKeeper cluster nodes and XD admin/container nodes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Kafka baseline benchmarking (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Run Kafka producer/consumer baseline benchmarks on the provisioned environment and record baseline throughput and latency figures for reference configurations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "XD use-case benchmarks and reporting (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Define and execute XD stream benchmarks (including the new offset, partitioning, and microbatching features), collect results, and produce a benchmark report.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Wiki documentation for new features (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Write and publish wiki documentation covering configuration of the new Kafka source offset options, partition pre-allocation, microbatching, the reactor-stream processor module, and the performance infrastructure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration testing and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Perform cross-feature end-to-end testing of complete streams combining the new capabilities, and fix defects discovered during integration and benchmark runs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 60
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Build, CI updates, and release packaging",
      "activity_description": "Update build and CI jobs to include the new modules and test suites, and package the increment (modules, distributions, docs) for release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 988
  }
}

